commit 1aa3d85fd701db53cefcb9a84f8787cd10283501
Author: María <mariagrandury@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 22 01:38:55 2026 +0200

    pretrain: pin the evaluated checkpoint set to twelve
    
    due_iters scaled the evaluated set with save density, so 1B evaluated 20
    checkpoints and 1.7B/3B 32, while ladder._on_shared_grid keeps only the
    ten tenths plus 85% and 95%. Measured over the planned grid: 824
    checkpoint-evals, of which 577 had already been computed and discarded
    and 247 were still to come -- 128 at 1B, 71 at 3B, 48 at 1.7B, none at
    600M or below, which were always on the tenths. due_iters now reads
    EVAL_GRID (10) instead of n_checkpoints(), returning exactly 12 at every
    density -- verified against the 20/40/60-save grids and aromanou's
    2,287-interval 1B, and asserted identical to the loader's benchmark set,
    which is the guarantee that nothing the analysis reads stops being
    produced. --every keeps its meaning as a coarsening factor but defaults
    to 1. The watchers now report eval DONE (12/12) for all 116 cells.
    
    Alongside, from the 3B audit:
    
    - Drop 24 planned-but-never-launched seed replicates (3,782 node-h).
      Every replicate ever trained is deep and no analysis reads a shallow
      seed std: the depth intervention's denominator is the deep baseline and
      the seed-holdout pools are deep scheme-A only. seeds_for() takes arch;
      the 1B triple loses L50. Nothing on disk is touched -- the two empty
      lm-1B-L30-schemeB-shallow dirs just fall out of the grid.
    - Register BT3 (scheme B at T=3, L30, deep, to 1.7B) so the data is not a
      blocker later. Registry only; no training is launched. A 92B target
      realizes 88.5B against the 83.6B a 1.7B draws, 0.94 epochs.
    - Carry the ZH undersized exception in the registry rather than a flag
      the operator had to retype, so the launcher is idempotent again, and
      name both ways out in the skip message.
    - Correct what the audit falsified: ITER_MS 3B 2300 -> 2120 (measured
      1,831-2,059 ms/iter wall, median 1,924, over 8 jobs; the logged
      1,814-1,832 omits the 60 saves, which is why these rungs are timed on
      wall-clock), the 3B cost ~1,900 -> ~1,630 node-h and the figures
      derived from it, the 20/40/60 checkpoint rule in both hyperparams
      globals and their generators, the width/depth claim in plan/models.md
      (51-78 across the ladder, not a rule pinning 64), the language-setting
      and data-scheme counts, and MIN_PER_TASK's stated rationale.
    - Extend check_rules rule 10 to the above-reference half, derived from
      ANALYSIS_SIZES so moving the reference moves the check. The external
      model pools are exempt: their "3B" is another project's model.

